rdingly and depending on how it  feels to you and while you're trying out  different monitor Heights  take note of your posture and take know  of whether you're straining your neck or  your shoulders or any other muscles all  of us have different bodies so there's  probably gonna be a good monitor height  that's different for all of us because  with everything in life and in tech it  depends  [Music]  so I think when a lot of people think  about ergonomics setups they often think  about standing desks now I've had mine  for a little over a year now and I feel  like they generally make me feel better  and Pat's got some interesting facts  about the relationship between desks and  ergonomics the science behind seated  desk height is pretty straightforward if  your desk sets you up to follow the 90  90 90 rule you're golden but starting  around 2012 more reports started coming  out about sitting as the new smoking  like if you sit all day you're gonna die  early so of course everybody panicked  okay we need some nuance here people who  spend most of the day seated have about  a 10 to 20 percent increased risk of  dying from heart disease that is a big  deal but people who smoke have about a  200 percent increased risk of dying from  heart disease so even that statistic  needs some more nuance attached to it  but no sitting is not smoking let's keep  that in mind  either way we do spend a lot of our  working hours seated so standing desks  became more popular and the research  followed after it now I know a couple  people who bought sit-stand desks and  never standed them they're always in the  seated position so a big question in the  research is how much of a difference do  these sit-stand desks actually make a  2018 study took 24 office workers in New  Zealand and swapped half of their seated  desks for electric adjustable height  desks basically a motorized sit-stand  desk all 24 of them track their activity  with pedometers and exercise Diaries and  that was it the